lantern-pr 1
# 47
#title Uninstall the Linux and Windows lantern command
#url https://github.com/MobileReality/lantern/pull/47
#branch feat/uninstall-lantern-cli-win-linux
#base feat/windows-installer
#opened 2026-11-13
#head ee47c94d7e09073d51a11535393119ae6e0bc4ab
#describe what Adds an uninstall for the lantern command on Linux and Windows that removes only what Lantern made.
#describe before The command could only be removed by hand.
#describe after Uninstall removes Lantern's link or shim and its PATH entry, leaves foreign commands and other PATH entries alone, and is a clean no-op when nothing is installed.
#describe verified Typecheck and the full test suite pass; new Linux and Windows uninstall tests failed before the code.
#plan windows-squirrel-installer s1.1
~ src/main/cli-user-install.ts
~ test/cli-user-install.test.ts
#order src/main/cli-user-install.ts
#order test/cli-user-install.test.ts
#reason src/main/cli-user-install.ts Lets the command be removed again without touching a link or shim Lantern did not create.
#reason test/cli-user-install.test.ts Pins uninstall so a left-behind link, shim or PATH entry fails the suite.
#story Removing the lantern command
#step actor A Linux or Windows user
#file src/main/cli-user-install.ts
#step action asks Lantern to remove the lantern command
#step subject the link or shim Lantern made
#file test/cli-user-install.test.ts
#below interaction Can undo the install and add it again later
#below consequence The command stays until removed by hand => Only Lantern's own link, shim and PATH entry go
